-- statement:
--   For a countable index set, L2(ι) is the complex Hilbert space of square-summable complex sequences on ι, a bijection of index sets induces a unitary reindexing between the corresponding L2 spaces, and l2Projection(p) is the norm-at-most-one coordinate projection that keeps entries where the predicate p holds and zeroes the rest. The model is a quantum spin system on the lattice Site(d)=ℤ^d with local levels Level(ℓ)={0,…,ℓ}, so spin ℓ/2. A Configuration is a finitely supported assignment of levels to sites, SpinHilbert(d,ℓ) is L2 of the configurations, and SpinOperator(d,ℓ) is the algebra of bounded operators on it. For a site x and levels a,b, matrixUnit(x,a,b) maps v to the function sending a configuration c to v(c with level b at x) when c(x)=a and to 0 otherwise, and operatorRelabel conjugates operators by a permutation of sites. The quasi-local algebra is the norm closure of the star-algebra generated by all these matrix units, and localUnit is the matrix unit viewed inside it. Translation by x is the star-endomorphism of the quasi-local algebra induced by relabeling sites by y↦x+y. With magnetic level m_k=k−ℓ/2, the spin operators at x are S^z=Σ_k m_k E_kk, the raising operator S^+ with coefficients √((ℓ/2)(ℓ/2+1)−m_k(m_k+1)) on E_{k+1,k}, S^-=(S^+)*, S^x=(S^++S^-)/2, and S^y=(S^+−S^-)/(2i). Nearest neighbors are sites at ℓ¹ distance 1, volumeEdges(Λ) lists each such pair in Λ once, using a well-ordering to orient it, and the finite-volume Hamiltonian is the negative of the sum over these edges of S^x S^x+S^y S^y+S^z S^z, a ferromagnetic Heisenberg model. box(d,n) is the cube [−n,n]^d. finiteDynamics(Λ,t) conjugates A by e^{itH_Λ}, dynamics is the limit of these along boxes as n→∞ (defined via limUnder, so it is arbitrary where no limit exists), and DynamicsConverges(d,ℓ) is the proposition that for every real t and every quasi-local A this convergence actually holds. A State is a norm-continuous linear functional on the quasi-local algebra with ω(1)=1 and ω(A*A) real and nonnegative for all A. TranslationInvariant(ω) means ω is unchanged by every translation. IsKMS(β,ω) means β>0 and, for all A and B, there is a bounded continuous function F on the strip 0≤Im z≤β, holomorphic in its interior, with F(t)=ω(A·dynamics_t(B)) and F(t+iβ)=ω(dynamics_t(B)·A) for all real t, the KMS condition at inverse temperature β for the infinite-volume dynamics.
